Third-party components, data, and attributions
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This product includes, depends on, or was trained using the following third-party
works. Each remains under its own license; the attributions below are provided for
informational purposes.

1. Prithvi-EO-2.0-300M foundation model
   Authors : NASA & IBM
   License : Apache License, Version 2.0
   Source  : https://huggingface.co/ibm-nasa-geospatial/Prithvi-EO-2.0-300M-TL
   Paper   : "Prithvi-EO-2.0: A Versatile Multi-Temporal Foundation Model for Earth
             Observation Applications", arXiv:2412.02732
   Use     : Frozen satellite-imagery encoder (LoRA fine-tuned). The base weights are the
             public Prithvi-EO-2.0-300M-TL checkpoint (unmodified, frozen), shipped inside the
             Model bundle; the architecture code is vendored as `prithvi_mae.py`.

2. HLS (Harmonized Landsat Sentinel-2) satellite imagery
   Source  : NASA / USGS (Landsat) and Copernicus / ESA (Sentinel-2)
   Use      : Input imagery composites, fetched live via Google Earth Engine.

3. Rainfall and temperature reanalysis (CHIRPS, ERA5)
   Use      : Dynamic weather features, fetched live via Google Earth Engine.

4. Open-Meteo forecast weather
   License  : CC-BY 4.0
   Use      : Forecast-window conditioning features, fetched live.

5. Groundwater-level observations
   Source   : Central Ground Water Board (CGWB) / India-WRIS / NWDP
   License  : Government Open Data License – India (GODL-India)
   Use      : Training targets/history and live "current" readings at inference.

6. Gemma (gemma3:4b) large language model
   Author   : Google
   License  : Gemma Terms of Use (https://ai.google.dev/gemma/terms)
   Use      : OPTIONAL — phrases the advisory's farmer-facing message when
              GWL_ADVISORY_SLM=1. Served locally via Ollama; NOT shipped or
              redistributed with this product. The advisory's decision and all
              numeric outputs are produced deterministically and are identical
              with or without Gemma (a built-in template is used when it is absent).

